{"t": "n", "id": "fct-zylyy3z6", "rev": 1, "kind": "fact", "key": null, "title": null, "body": "The Epoch 2 boundary audit split its 94 functions over cognitive 15 by `git blame` at HEAD and named 8 «the fork's». All 8 were upstream-authored: the upstream syncs land as the fork's own commits («operator pre-CI commit»), so blame names the fork for lines it took unchanged — five of the 8 were byte-identical to upstream at `547d7514b`, and the other three read upstream's own score. Blame also missed the fork's real growth inside upstream bodies, where the fork's lines are a minority: comparing each function's score with the same file and name at the last synced upstream rev (rust-code-analysis-cli on `git show {rev}:{path}`) found 13 carrying fork-added complexity, `build_accessibility_node` at 50 against upstream's 19. Measure the fork's share by that comparison, never by blame.\n\n", "data": {"fam": "harness"}}
